issue('SURVEY_01','Fuel capacity and tank shape are configuration-dependent','HB pp. 9,29,33; Jordan pp. 27,29','Preliminary: 3 × 80 gallons, total 240. Production account: 3 × 50 gallons, total 150. Capacity alone does not fix shell geometry.','Keep distinct preliminary and production fuel assemblies. For Rock Island blockout use production capacity as a constraint, not a scale factor applied to the preliminary tank drawing.','variant_separation')
issue('SURVEY_02','Machine guns and stowage cannot be merged across configurations','HB pp. 9,171,175,180,182; Jordan p. 27; SNL pp. 223-225','HB gives seven Hotchkiss machine guns with inconsistent enumerated positions; Jordan gives five Brownings. Ammunition totals also differ. SNL names Browning platform ammunition storage.','Select armament by configuration. Preserve all alternatives and use production photographs/installation drawings before placing ball mounts.','variant_separation')
issue('SURVEY_03','Carburetor change runs in both directions over time','Jordan pp. 29,32; SNL p. 57 and note (gx), p. 309; LIB pp. 43-60','Jordan describes replacing Zenith with Ball & Ball during production; SNL orders Zenith substitution under O.C.M. 2344, 1 September 1922. The aircraft manual also has Claudel-Hobson H.C.7.','Use Ball & Ball for a supported production representation and modified U.S. No. 52 Zenith for a later service alternative. Do not assume H.C.7 was installed in the tank.','resolved_chronology')
issue('SURVEY_04','Electrical counts and voltages in Jordan conflict with technical catalog','Jordan p. 29; HB pp. 160-170; SNL pp. 14,100,123','Jordan lists one 12-V ignition generator, two 6-V generators, two 12-V batteries and one 6-V battery. SNL lists one 8-V Delco generator, one 12-V Bijur generator, a Bijur starting motor, SYR-13 ignition battery and two STR-4 starting/lighting batteries.','Do not build a circuit or physical equipment count from Jordan alone. Use HB wiring and SNL for a dated technical fit; leave historical origin of Jordan wording unresolved.')
issue('SURVEY_05','Lower crankcase bearing counts appear reversed in one assembly','SNL p. 17 versus p. 58; LIB p. 17','SNL individual entries give LQ238A long lower bearing quantity 1 and LQ240A short quantity 6; p. 58 composed-of list gives six LQ238A long and one LQ240A short. Upper halves on p. 59 and LIB front/rear bearing description support one long and six short.','High-confidence proposed correction to the p. 58 association: one long and six short. Raw source edges retained; do not silently edit them.','proposed_high_confidence',marks=['LQ238A','LQ240A','LQ239A','LQ241A'],category='quantity',source='SNL')
issue('SURVEY_06','Road-track wheel and chain sprocket diameter must be separated','HB pp. 130,132,136','The 23.031 value on p. 136 conflicts with the road-track wheel dimensions on p. 130 and matches its chain-sprocket diameter.','Use 39.237-inch outside / 32.75-inch inside for the road-track wheel as printed on p. 130; reserve 23.031 inches for the chain sprocket. p. 136 remains an apparent label error.','proposed_high_confidence',marks=['M1401','M1404','M1540'],category='dimension',source='HB')
issue('SURVEY_07','Pistons differ between aircraft, original tank and replacement','LIB pp. 13-16,109; HB p. 203; SNL pp. 146,165,309-310','Aircraft domed/flat pistons, LQ466A original tank piston and SH1020A replacement must not become one shape. LQ469A ring position is contradictory.','Retain three configuration contexts and unresolved ring location. Tank crown/compression geometry needs exact drawing.','variant_separation',marks=['LQ466A','SH1020A','LQ469A'])
issue('SURVEY_08','Exact manufacturing piece census is unavailable from the catalog alone','SNL note (b), p. 308; note (gy), p. 310; note (gam), p. 310','Some commercial subassembly internals are explicitly omitted; certain supplier products are listed only as units; the spare/accessory addendum is announced for Changes No. 1.','Survey covers all preserved table rows and named supplemental objects. Unlisted internals remain scope gaps, never a claim of zero parts.','documented_limit',category='coverage',source='SNL')
issue('SURVEY_09','Roller total is not 58 plus 28','HB p. 136; SNL p. 197 and note (gp), p. 309','There are 58 lower rollers total, with 28 spring-equipped and 30 plain in HB. SNL note (gp) explains 58 total and 28 when assembled with flange.','58 is the inclusive lower-roller total. Do not sum nested SNL assembly quantities. Upper rollers are a separate pair.','resolved_scope',category='quantity')
issue('SURVEY_10','Sponson stowage requires gun/mount reconfiguration','Alden specification pp. 1-2, Figs. 1-3; GUN p. 21, Plate X; HB Plate 130','Patent shows sponson pivoting inward; gun manual describes a distinct transport arrangement with bracket A, altered gun position and coordinated traverse.','A rigid deployed gun attached to a simply rotating sponson is not a validated stowage animation. Model the transport state and test swept clearance after calibration.','documented_constraint',category='kinematic')
issue('SURVEY_11','Power and reverse-speed summaries disagree','HB p. 9, Plates 74-77; Jordan p. 27','HB gives 338 hp at 1400 rpm and two reverse speeds. Jordan says approximately 400 hp at 1400 rpm and one reverse speed; HB plates illustrate high/low reverse.','Use explicit transmission mechanism evidence for kinematic blockout; retain reported ratings as source claims. Do not infer dimensional changes from the power values.','open',category='specification')
issue('SURVEY_12','Plate scale is not a reliable engineering scale without calibration','HB general arrangement and dimensional plates; SNL restored plates','Restored, dewarped and resized figures have no new measurement authority. SNL Plate 2 aspect ratio remains uncertain.','Retain original-to-derivative transforms, calibrate independent axes with printed dimensions and record residuals before accepting traced coordinates.','documented_limit',category='geometry')
issue('SURVEY_13','Belleville spring dimensional record is physically inconsistent','SNL pp. 138,219; note (gh), p. 309','SH642B outside diameter is smaller than its inside diameter on p. 219; both thickness readings are suspect. Note (gh) permits one Thrackray washer in place of three springs but supplies no correction.','No numerical correction adopted. Seek drawing or measure surviving assembly.','open',marks=['SH642B'],category='dimension',source='SNL')
issue('SURVEY_14','Drawing references with suffix letters are not part marks','SNL pp. 116,144,165','213A accompanies M772; 679A accompanies M280, M270, M285 and M273. A leading-numeric Ordnance reference cannot become the canonical part key.','Use the British piece mark for those identities; retain drawing reference separately. This is a schema/extraction rule, not source errata.','resolved_schema',marks=['M772','M280','M270','M285','M273'],category='identity',source='SNL')
issue('SURVEY_15','Gauge counts and ration boxes include unrealized future-production alternatives','SNL notes (gt),(gv), p. 309','First 100 tanks use four pressure gauges versus three specified for future production; box provision likewise changes.','Future production is a stated alternative, not evidence that a second production batch existed.','variant_separation',category='configuration',source='SNL')

